markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Flowchart Comparison

Below are two flowcharts that show iteration in action.
Before labeling them, take a moment to study how each one repeats.
---


## Flowchart A

<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:24px; margin:20px 0px;">

  <img src="https://images.code.org/d80a0b774a89fa285465c1a50a654d79-image-1768419690819.png" alt="flowchart for a for loop" style="width:38%; max-width:350px; border-radius:10px;">

  <div style="flex:1; min-width:0;">

**Think about:**

- What causes the steps to repeat?
- Is the number of repetitions fixed?
- What makes the loop stop?

👉 **Which type of loop do you think this represents?**

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">💡 Check your thinking:</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;">

  <div style="margin-top:16px; margin-left:14px; margin-right:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:12pt; line-height:1.4;">
      Flowchart A represents a <b>count-controlled loop (for loop)</b> because the number of repetitions is determined in advance.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

  </div>
</div>

<div style="clear:both;"></div>
---
## Flowchart B

<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:24px; margin:20px 0px;">

  <img src="https://images.code.org/4afcb2bde4184c0c4735dcfb18d4a4a2-image-1768418982827.png" alt="flowchart for a while loop" style="width:38%; max-width:350px; border-radius:10px;">

  <div style="flex:1; min-width:0;">

**Think about:**

- Does the loop repeat a known number of times?
- Is the number of repetitions fixed?
- Or does it continue until a condition changes?

👉 **Which type of loop do you think this represents?**

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">💡 Check your thinking:</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;">

  <div style="margin-top:16px; margin-left:14px; margin-right:14px;">
    <p style="font-size:12pt; line-height:1.4;">
      Flowchart B represents a <b>condition-controlled loop (while loop)</b> because the steps repeat as long as a condition remains true.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>

  </div>
</div>



## Next up

Let's see what this looks like in code starting with for loops. 




MARKDOWN
